 so you pay no unusual premium for downside protection or for upside calls.\n\nPrice alone gives no strong reason to add or to hold back. Whether to add depends on your view of VLTX demand. Utilities make up 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham Power is 35% of utility orders and Norvane is 21%, so two customers drive a large share of the business. That concentration is a risk to the position, and it's separate from how the options are priced. The demand and financing questions are with n2 and n3.\n\nI only checked implied volatility, skew and customer mix. I did not check the underlying price, the specific strikes and expiries, or the options' Greeks.\n\nSources: the `vltx-leaps` and `vltx-order-mix` documents and the `vltx_iv_history` series.","ttft_ms":2715,"type":"result","duration_ms":19350,"uuid":"56f363ab-bdfd-43e9-9b1a-1cea84f1c73f","ttft_stream_ms":1955,"time_to_request_ms":692,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":67,"system_prompt":31,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":14,"input_attachments":81,"input_hooks":28,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":137,"tool_pool_refresh":43,"init_message":70,"init_frame_send":22,"engine_pickup":17,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":33,"request_announcements":53,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":11,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":24,"client_creation":10,"request_build":23},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":348,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":102,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":173,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":98,"process_rss_mib_result":190,"process_anon_mib_result":108,"process_peak_rss_mib":190,"process_cpu_ms_turn":527,"process_wall_ms_turn":19327,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":44,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1217,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_count":123,"main_stream_chunk_count":12,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":44,"wall_ms":1217,"entries":3},"tool":{"cpu_ms":186,"wall_m